From 2201139167a5e3d7b2047d426ce0238d78cce48a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yibo Wang <2024312277@stu.hit.edu.cn>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 05:37:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: compute power_now on kaanapali

The OPPO kaanapali battery firmware does not follow the reference
rate semantics for BATT_POWER_NOW: the raw value neither scales with
voltage*current nor tracks the load (verified across charging and
discharging regimes - it is near-constant while real power changed
2x, previously surfacing as a bogus ~88W power_now).

For the OPLUS_BATTMGR_KAANAPALI variant, fetch fresh voltage and
current readings and report their product, with the sign following
the battery current (positive while charging). The product of uV and
uA overflows 32 bits, so compute in 64 bits.

Verified on the device: power_now now tracks V*I within 0.3%
across load changes, e.g. -7.16W vs -7.15W hand-computed while
discharging at ~1.95A.
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 819e300fbe79..088bd68675ec 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -588,6 +588,30 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_bat_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.current_now;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_POWER_NOW:
+		if (battmgr->variant == OPLUS_BATTMGR_KAANAPALI) {
+			/*
+			 * The OPPO kaanapali battery firmware does not follow
+			 * the reference rate semantics: the raw value neither
+			 * scales with voltage*current nor tracks the load.
+			 * Compute the power from fresh voltage and current
+			 * readings instead, with the sign following the
+			 * battery current (positive while charging).
+			 */
+			ret = qcom_battmgr_bat_sm8350_update(battmgr,
+						     POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW);
+			if (ret < 0)
+				return ret;
+			ret = qcom_battmgr_bat_sm8350_update(battmgr,
+						     POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW);
+			if (ret < 0)
+				return ret;
+
+			/* uV * uA overflows 32 bits; result in uW */
+			val->intval = div_s64((s64)battmgr->status.voltage_now *
+					      battmgr->status.current_now,
+					      1000000);
+			break;
+		}
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.power_now;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN:
